<style>
  /* Demo page — built from the site tokens (carbon / toxic / Oxanium). */
  .demo-hero { margin: 0 0 30px; }
  .demo-hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 32px;
    line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--carbon); margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .demo-hero p { font-size: 17px; color: var(--graphite); max-width: 56ch; margin: 0; }
  .demo-hero .rule {
    height: 3px; width: 110px; margin-top: 16px; border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--toxic), var(--toxic-muted) 60%, transparent);
  }

  .demo-tool {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 24px; margin: 0 0 20px;
    box-shadow: -3px 0 0 0 var(--toxic), 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
  }
  .demo-tool-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .content .demo-title { display: flex; align-items: center; margin: 0; padding: 0; border: 0; line-height: 1; }
  .demo-logo { height: 44px; width: auto; display: block; }
  .demo-wordmark {
    font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 28px;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: #1a1a1a; line-height: 1;
  }
  .demo-tool > p { margin: 0 0 10px; max-width: 62ch; }
  .demo-lead { font-size: 16px; color: var(--carbon); }
  .model-note { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--slate); margin-top: -2px; }

  /* Quiet light-grey blocks built from --mist, so commands sit inside the page
     rather than cutting it into dark slabs. A hairline toxic edge keeps them ours. */
  .cmd {
    background: var(--mist); color: var(--carbon);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--toxic-muted);
    border-radius: 8px; padding: 13px 16px; margin: 6px 0 14px;
    font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .demo-cases { list-style: none; margin: 4px 0 12px; padding: 0; }
  .demo-cases li { padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 15px; color: var(--graphite); }
  .demo-cases li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .demo-cases a { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .demo-cases a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .demo-links { font-size: 14px; color: var(--slate); margin: 6px 0 0; }
  .demo-links a { text-decoration: none; }
  .demo-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>

<div class="main">
  <div class="content">

    <div class="demo-hero">
      <h1>Run the stack yourself</h1>
      <p>Three tools. Everything runs locally — no account, key, or GPU.</p>
      <div class="rule"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="demo-tool" id="scan" aria-labelledby="scan-title">
      <div class="demo-tool-head">
        <h2 class="demo-title" id="scan-title"><img class="demo-logo" src="/assets/images/scan.svg" alt="Scan"></h2>
        <span class="badge badge-stable">stable</span>
      </div>

      <p class="demo-lead">Local malware detection, powered by offline AI models.</p>

      <p>Install,</p>
<pre class="cmd">curl -fsSL https://install.atomdrift.org/scan.sh | sh</pre>

<p>scan a known-good binary:</p>

<pre class="cmd">atomscan /bin/ls</pre>

      <p>0-day demo — 12 fresh samples across Go, npm, Java, PE, VSCode, PyPI:</p>
<pre class="cmd">curl -LO https://atomdrift.org/demo/samples.zip
atomscan samples.zip</pre>

      <div class="admonition warning">
        <p>NOTE: samples.zip contains encrypted malware, please execute atomscan in a location that won't alarm your security team.</p>
      </div>

      <p>Also worth testing is the <code>--llm</code> flag, which blends a large language model's read with the local ML verdict. Any
      OpenAI-compatible endpoint works:</p>
<pre class="cmd">atomscan --llm ${URL} samples.zip</pre>

      <p class="demo-links"><a href="https://atomdrift.org/scan/">Scan Overview</a>
      &middot; <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/scan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-tool" id="lab" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
      <div class="demo-tool-head">
        <h2 class="demo-title" id="lab-title"><span class="demo-wordmark">lab / fallout</span></h2>
        <span class="badge badge-stable">stable</span>
      </div>

      <p class="demo-lead">Recent catches from auditing 175+ software sources. Each
      is mapped to a &ldquo;mal-ecule&rdquo;: a fingerprint of what a sample does, not its bytes.</p>

      <ul class="demo-cases">
        <li><a href="https://lab.atomdrift.org/file/a4516971edc3493f7dc66f8310e6b42627b22dfb915882c169dda5550cb52b17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A worked example</a> — one sample, decomposed</li>
        <li><a href="https://lab.atomdrift.org/fallout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The fallout feed</a> — everything caught, live</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="demo-links"><a href="https://lab.atomdrift.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the Lab &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-tool" id="isomer" aria-labelledby="isomer-title">
      <div class="demo-tool-head">
        <h2 class="demo-title" id="isomer-title"><img class="demo-logo" src="/assets/images/isomer.svg" alt="isomer"></h2>
        <span class="badge badge-experimental">experimental</span>
      </div>

      <p class="demo-lead">Detects whether a <em>change</em> is malicious. The version
      says nothing changed; the behavior says otherwise. No release binary yet, so it needs a Rust compiler:</p>
<pre class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/atomdrift-project/isomer.git
cd isomer
make demo</pre>

      <p><code>make demo</code> runs four real attacks as old&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;new pairs.</p>     <ul>
        <li><a href="https://isotope13.ai/compendium/2024/xzutils/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">xz-utils</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://isotope13.ai/compendium/2025/rand-user-agent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rand-user-agent</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://isotope13.ai/compendium/2026/node-ipc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">node-ipc</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://isotope13.ai/compendium/2009/unrealircd/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UnrealIRCd</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p>You can use <code>LLM_URL</code> to point isomer at your own endpoint for large language model interpretation.</p>

      <p class="demo-links"><a href="https://atomdrift.org/isomer/">Overview</a>
      &middot; <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/isomer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></p>
    </section>

  </div>

